// expect: error[VN3021]
//
// Caught by the checker, not the VM: an all-literal arithmetic expression whose
// value leaves the `int` range is reported at its own span, before the program
// runs. The run-time raise (int-overflow-mul.vn) stays the guarantee; this is
// the earlier, better-located warning.
//
// `int` is a native i64, so the operands have to be genuinely enormous. Two
// values just above 2^32 whose product passes 2^63.
const squared = 4000000000 * 4000000000
print(squared)
